WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.202
[MUSIC]

00:00:10.202 --> 00:00:14.678
If you think about the speed
at which a crisis develops,

00:00:14.678 --> 00:00:17.822
far faster than it ever did before, and

00:00:17.822 --> 00:00:22.980
so you may not have all
the information you would like.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:28.070
You may not know all the facts and

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:31.610
that might lead you to not respond.

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:34.830
There's a natural tendency, well,
we don't have all the facts so

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:36.160
we can't really say anything.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:40.280
Well, what you can say
is what your values are.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:42.850
And what you can talk about your values,
and

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:47.790
that whatever you do in response to a
particular crisis is going to be based on

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:50.990
the values of your organization or
your company.

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:55.980
Companies that don't really have
clarity about their values and

00:00:55.980 --> 00:01:01.390
are kind of coming up with them on the
fly, they're at a tremendous disadvantage.

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:06.090
Conversely, companies that have
a very clear sense of who they are,

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:11.939
what they stand for, even in the midst of
crisis, they have competitive advantage.

00:01:11.939 --> 00:01:19.295
[MUSIC]

